        "title": "Not worth it for Non-Hindus",
        "text": "1000 RPN entrance fee for foreigners. If you can prove you’re Hindu or Indian it’s free (ie. passport or citizen card or some sort of identification). Non-Hindu people are not allowed in the main temple. There isn’t much to do in the area. Witnessing the cremations would be the biggest highlight, but I personally thought it was weird that such a private matter (mourning the death of a loved one and preparing their cremation ceremony) was publicized at a UNESCO World Heritage site, where tourists are snapping photos and exploring around. Anyway, it’s definitely once in a lifetime experience but I didn’t think it was worth 1000 RPN. It can be emotional seeing the bodies and cremation ceremonies. It’s sad to see the river, where the ashes are poured in, is completely polluted with plastic bottles and garbage which are mainly due to the local children who play in and around the river. ",
