        "title": "Witness a Hindu Cremation Ceremony First-Hand",
        "text": "The entrance fee to this temple was very exorbitant at Rs1000. However, I found it worth it because I got to witness a Hindi cremation ceremony first-hand. I went down to get a closer look and saw how they dressed the deceased and how his family and the priest went about the ceremony. It was long - around 1 hour. You can't take photos or videos of the cremation ceremony up close though.\n\nYou can see the holy river too and where they cremate the bodies in fire and throw the ashes into the river. There are also some monkeys here.\n\nAs a tourist, you can't go inside the main temple of Shiva so that's disappointing for how much you paid.",
