      {
        "review_id": 632730958,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r632730958-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "UNESCO Cultural World Heritage Site",
        "text": "Pashupatinath is an incredibly important site for Nepali, being a religious site of observance for over 1000 years. Here a series of different aged temples line the river where ghats smoulder with funeral pyres. As a functioning cremation site there are funerals occurring continually at the site; so expect to see cremains, pyres, and sacred purification rituals occurring along the river banks. Foreigners pay NPR 1000 each that goes toward maintenance and restoration as some temples were damaged in the 2015 earthquakes. The day we visited the palls of smoke were recognisable on the walk to the entrance and the ashen smell will follow you throughout the visit. Fascinating to observe the Hindu and Buddhist faith as experienced through their mourning. Challenging, and fascinating site.",
        "review_tip": null,
